## AI action log (`../ai_#N.log`)

- Global enable flag `DAT_01027180` (byte, never written by game code — developer switch); `DAT_01027181` = no flush.
  Enabled by `src/patches/AiLogs.cpp`.
- At map start `FUN_00B610B0(mapName)` (called from `0x007E0AD6` and `0x008099C9`) opens the 8 slots only if the flag
  is set; existing files are deleted first.
- Row writer gate `FUN_00B610E0`: flag set, player at `[this+0x70]` is AI (player vtable `+0x18C`), slot = player
  number (vtable `+0x2C`) - 1.
- 8 per-player log slots at `0x010271A8 + 0x24 * n`, initialised by `FUN_00B60340` (file `../ai_#%i.log`, relative to `bin`).
- Writer `FUN_00B603F0` (one row per call; format below).
- Check `FUN_00B60320` returns the flag (used e.g. by market trading logs).

## AI log file structure and analysis

Written in the game root (`G:\__H5__\H5Xdev\ai_#N.log`, N = player number). Tab-separated text, CRLF, ANSI
(read as latin-1). Line 1 = column header, line 2 = `Log starts <date> on map <map> for AI player N (<color>),
<difficulty>`, then one row per event. Typical size: ~300 rows per AI day (6 days ≈ 1800 rows, 320 KB).

### Columns

| Column | Content |
|---|---|
| `Date` | `month,week,day (absolute day index)`, e.g. `1,1,3 (2)` |
| `Hero` | `<name> L<level> <role>`, role: `Com` = Commander, `Fre` = Freelancer, `Col(<hero>)` = Collector for that hero, `Sup(<hero>)` = Supplier for that hero (see `Roles*` parameters) |
| `Town` | `<town name> L<town level>` (town rows only) |
| `Cell` | `x,y,floor` of the hero/town; destination and movement rows use `from => to` |
| `Tag` | Row type (see below) |
| `Action` | What happens (`visit`, `capture`, `meet`, `fight win …`, step name and timing, …) |
| `Object` | Target object or detail (object name, creature stack, skill/perk, building `TB_*`, `Winner army … \| Loser army … \| Winner hero …` for fights) |
| `ObjInfo` | Extra info on the target, e.g. `(owned by player 0) \| (dock deserted) \|` |
| `Value` | AI value of the destination/choice (float). Destination values of all kinds are compared directly |
| `Money` | Cost or gain of the action (`4 ore, 500 gold`, `5 wood`) |
| `Gold` … `Gem` | Treasury after the row: `<amount> + <daily income> (<AI value of one unit>)`, e.g. `52 + 2 (1461)`; unit values are recomputed from demand/supply after day 1 |
| `Heroes`, `Towns` | Number of heroes and towns owned |

### Row types (`Tag`)

| Tag | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `step` | A turn step finished: `<STEP>: <ms> ms, <n> cmds` |
| `step ->` | Next step chosen for a hero (`MOVE_HERO`, `START_CHOOSE_DESTINATION`, …) |
| (empty) | Day-start housekeeping timings (`Clear pathfinders`, `Solve puzzlemap`, `CHeck threats`) |
| `selected` | `Wave spread: search limit = <cost>, time = <ms>` — start of a destination search. The limit is a movement-cost budget: `700` = `RolesSearchNearMaxCost`, `32000` = `RolesSearchFarMaxCost`, other values (1500, 3000, …) computed elsewhere (origin unknown) |
| `estimate` | Search/choice results: `found <n> destinations`, `no destinations found`, `no suitable destination found, search not finished`, `not reach any target this turn`, level-up candidates (`available skill/perk: … (mastery m, value v)`), town building wishes (`build: want` / `build: gain points` + `TB_*`), `calculated hire heroes races coefs` |
| `destination (new best)` | Candidate destination that beats the current best (`Value` = its score) |
| `destination (discarded, A <= B)` | Candidate scored `A`, below the best `B` |
| `destination (discarded bonus, n >= n)` / `(discarded not bonus, because not positive (v))` / `(discarded neutral for positive previous)` | Other rejection rules (bonus-visit limit, non-positive value, …) |
| `do` | Action actually ordered: `visit`, `visits`, `capture`, `captures flagged`, `meet`, `builds`, `builds upgrade`, `purchases`, `hires hero`, `level up` (+ attribute), `begin day`, `end turn: <steps> steps, <s> seconds` |
| `done` | Result: `fight win (<our power> vs <their power>), <x>% lost [(survive cheat)]`, `got artifact`, `gets money`, `level up` (selected skill/perk), `heroes met`, `pursues fleeing monster` |

`(survive cheat)` marks fights where the AI's difficulty bonus cancels its losses.

### What to analyze

- **Destination choice** — filter `destination*` rows: which target types are considered (`Action` + `Object`), their
  `Value`, and why others were discarded. This is where "the AI ignores X" shows: a target type that never appears as a
  candidate is not generated by `BUILD_HERO_CHOICES` / the destination search; one that appears with a low `Value` is
  under-scored by the estimator.
- **Search range** — ratio of `no destinations found` / `search not finished` to `found <n> destinations`, and the
  `search limit` values: heroes that find nothing nearby stop exploring.
- **Executed actions** — `do` rows per hero and role, compared with the candidates: what the AI really spends moves on.
- **Fights** — `done` / `fight win` rows: power ratio, losses, `survive cheat`; who is fought (only blockers/guards vs
  deliberate clearing).
- **Pickups** — `got artifact`, `gets money`, `capture`: count per day vs what lies around the start area.
- **Economy and town** — `builds`, `purchases`, `build: want`, treasury columns (income growth, unit values).
- **Turn cost** — `end turn: … steps, … seconds` and per-step `ms`: needed before making the search wider.

### First log (H5X_Stadium, normal difficulty, AI player 2 Necropolis, days 1–6)

- Destination candidates are only `visit` (583), `meet` (20) and `capture` (15): **attacking a neutral stack is never a
  destination**. The 18 fights all happen on the way (16 with `survive cheat`), so clearing neutrals around the town
  cannot happen with the current choice building.
- Median values: `meet` hero 0.6M–2.2M (up to 7.5M) ≫ `capture` Ore Pit ~250k / Sawmill ~84k ≫ `visit` Ore ~108k /
  Wood ~67k ≫ Campfire ~24k / Dolmen of Knowledge ~15k ≫ Windmill ~2k / Temple 5. Joining armies dominates everything.
- 141 searches end with `no destinations found` or `search not finished`, against 107 `found <n> destinations`:
  searches often return nothing.
- Turns: 15–34 steps, 8–16 s per day.

## Data parameters — `RPGStats/AI/Adventure` in `GameMechanics/RPGStats/DefaultStats.xdb`

Type registered by `FUN_009511A0`. Overridden by H5X in `data/h5x-core.pak`.

- Per difficulty (`DifficultyEasy/Normal/Hard/Heroic`): `AttackHumanAggressivityCoef`, `AttackComputerAggressivityCoef`,
  `CowardiceVersusHuman/Computer`, `RolesSearchNear/FarMaxCost`, `ArmyPowerCoefBonusPerHeroLevel`, `ValueOfTown`,
  `AvengerVersusHuman/ComputerCoef`, `TownBuildPeriodInDays`, `CheckTownsInDanger`, `CheckHeroesDanger`,
  `ConsiderGarrisoningHeroToImportantTown`, `HireHeroesBase/PerTown/GlobalLimit`, `GrailSearch*`, `Threats*`,
  `StrategicCaptureDistance`, `TownCreatureGrowthCoef`.
- Global: `Search*` (destination search), `Roles*` (hero roles Commander / Collector / Supplier / Freelancer),
  `SupplyDayIncomes`, `Creature*Coef` (army strength estimate), ~30 `ValueOf*`, `Siege*`, `CollectPathBonuses*`,
  `Necromancy_*`.
- H5X vs ToE (as of this survey, set on purpose to push the AI toward exploring instead of rushing — see
  "Problems to fix"): aggressivity 1 → 0.5, cowardice → 0.3, `AvengerVersusComputerCoef` → 0,
  most `CreatureOver*` / luck / morale coefs → 0.000001, `ValueOfTown` ×4, threat parameters raised.

Combat AI parameters are in the sibling section `RPGStats/AI/Combat`.
